# "promise" was considered for a shift. In "universal" it could mean merely uttering promise-words; in "promise_possible" it could mean a promise that is taken up and believed.
# But the maxim (S4) is to get money by a promise the lender accepts. So the maxim's "promise" already needs promises to be credited, and A1 uses the same sense: no bridge.
# "end" in promise_possible is the aim one has in promising. It is used only in that sense.
